<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Torquato Tasso</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1544–<a href="/years/1595">1595</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Torquato Tasso was an Italian poet who served at the court of Duke <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alfonso-ii-deste">Alfonso II d'Este</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ferrara">Ferrara</a>. His epic <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jerusalem">Jerusalem</a> Delivered, completed in 1575, tells of the First Crusade and became one of the most widely read poems in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a>. Suffering from mental illness, he was confined in the hospital of Sant'Anna in Ferrara from 1579 to 1586.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/torquato-tasso.jpg" alt="Torquato Tasso" width="320" height="471" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Jacopo Bassano · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Torquato_Tasso,_aged_22,_by_Jacopo_da_Ponte,_called_Jacopo_Bassano_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
